e8-themes NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

This is the news of e8-themes, Emacs's most used themes ported to E8.
'C-h P' shows it under the package's description.


* Changes in e8-themes 0.2.1

** Leuven's text is no longer drawn too small to read.

** Zenburn and doom-manegarm keep all their colours.
Two of their palette's names had become one, and one colour replaced
the other.

** Nord colours 26 more faces, 'org-verbatim' among them.

** 'e8-themes-select' stays readable under every theme.
Its own text no longer uses the 'shadow' face, and its lines neither
wrap nor fold.


* Changes in e8-themes 0.2.0

** The collection grows from 20 themes to 168.
The Modus themes come from modus-themes 5.3.0, and the 40 Ef themes,
63 of Doom's, 25 from solarized-emacs, 14 of GNU Emacs 31.1's own, and
more of Gruvbox, Tomorrow and Catppuccin are new.

** Each Catppuccin flavour is a theme, 'catppuccin-latte' and the rest.
'catppuccin' still follows 'catppuccin-flavor'.

** '/' in 'e8-themes-select' narrows the list as you type.
Words match the start of a word in a theme's name, collection,
description or authors, and "dark" and "light" match the background.

** 'e8-themes-select' shows each theme's authors, source and contrast.

** 'e8-themes-select' opens at once, loading no theme until it shows.

** THEMES.md credits every theme, and says which were left out and why.


* Changes in e8-themes 0.1.0

This is the first release: twenty themes, and a chooser.

** 'M-x e8-themes-select' shows each theme as you move through them.
Beside the list is a sample of code, Org and a diff in the theme.

** 'n' and 'p' move, 'RET' keeps the theme, and 'q' goes back.

** 'TAB' shows only the dark themes, then only the light, then all.

** The Modus themes, Leuven and Wombat are there as Emacs ships them.

** Gruvbox, Solarized, Tomorrow, Catppuccin, Zenburn and Dracula too.

** Doom One, Doom One Light and Doom Tokyo Night are ported.

** Nord comes from e8-nord-theme, with its options.

** 'M-x catppuccin-load-flavor' changes Catppuccin's flavour.
